@{
    ViewBag.Title = "About IndoDex";
}
<h2>@ViewBag.Title.</h2>
<h3>Necessity truly is the mother of invention</h3>

<p>Over the years I have had to remember a massive amount of information on a number of topics and
    it's hard to recal this information all of the time.  That combined with speedy and sometimes sloppy 
    note taking lead to the creation of this tool (Information Rolodex) to help manage and retrieve these details.<p>
 <p>InfoDex uses an <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/N-gram">n-gram</a> searching algorithm against several 
    Microsoft Access databases to generate a Hits rating of each data entry and listing answer candidates in 
    descending order.  Each entry can be viewed, updated or deleted.  Why Micrsoft Access databases?  Because I wanted this
    tool to be somewhat portable and Everyone knows Access.  In fact, I have ported foreign data sources (such as Email)
    into an InfoDex database in order to make the data "more searchable".</p>
<p>I have had several software development jobs sectors such as Telecommunications, Oil and Gas, Human Resource Management,
    Real Time Data Acquisition and Control ... and have used InfoDex in each of these poistions and have found it invaluable.</p>
<p>
    How does seaching work?  InfoDex uses an n-gram algorithm to find patterns of characters within stored data resulting in
    hit tallies.<br />
    
